00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.010
Because you can remember water
molecules are surrounding the ions here.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:53.280
So there's only so many water molecules
available to surround all these molecules.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.869
This is, there's more to be
dissolved is what unsaturated means.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:04.280
Saturated is when you reach the maximum
threshold for the solute to be dissolved.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:05.830
So that's saturated.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.250
So that is like, unsaturated
is like, not sweet enough.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.500
Saturated is just right.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.920
This is like, okay, the
Goldilocks situation.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.529
This is right where you want it to be.

00:03:15.529 --> 00:03:17.470
You don't want it to
go any more, any less.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.310
It tastes perfect the way it is.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:26.750
Now super saturated is when it goes
way beyond what it's able to handle.

00:03:27.019 --> 00:03:31.640
So that means that you are way above
