they bounce all over the place.

00:15:28.685 --> 00:15:33.015
And the more kinetic energy they have, the
higher the temperature, the more they're

00:15:33.015 --> 00:15:34.955
going to actually bounce as a result.

00:15:35.435 --> 00:15:39.024
One way to think of it as an analogy
is imagine giving like a five year

00:15:39.024 --> 00:15:41.824
old about 10 pounds of candy, right?

00:15:41.824 --> 00:15:43.504
They're going to be
running around like crazy.

00:15:43.804 --> 00:15:46.724
Well, the higher the temperature
goes, the more those gas

00:15:46.724 --> 00:15:47.954
molecules are going to move.

00:15:48.255 --> 00:15:51.074
And they're going to continue
to kind of bounce around like a

00:15:51.074 --> 00:15:54.974
little ping pong ball, like going
all over the place as a result.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.780
So, the more, the hotter it gets,
the more of a problem that is.

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:03.430
Now, in terms of a bigger
effect, that could have a huge,

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.239
even global effect as well.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:08.360
Global warming is one of the big
issues that we're always bringing

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.719
up in the scientific community.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:13.739
The hotter the earth gets, the more,
the less oxygen that's actually going

00:16:13.739 --> 00:16:16.320
to be dissolved inside of water.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:22.090
So, in terms of aqua, uh, marine
wildlife that relies on oxygen to live.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:26.110
The hotter and hotter it gets, the
less oxygen there is, meaning the

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:29.920
less fish or even the smaller size
that they will be when they grow.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.519
It can be a really big issue.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:35.130
So let's take a look at some other
things as well when it comes to this too.

00:16:35.159 --> 00:16:37.340
The other part has to do
with not only temperature of

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:39.049
gases, but the pressure too.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.460
So gases are, they're always
under pressure all the time,

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:44.170
just like students and ourselves.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:48.390
So the solubility of a great
gas increases with pressure.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.770
